speechtext:
For a return showing-
1.	The total amount paid in compensation in the province of Nova Scotia, for animals slaughtered under the Animals Contagious Disease Act, termed The Health of Animals, in each of the years ending March 31, 1926, 1927, and 1928;
2.	The amount of compensation paid for cattle slaughtered as re-actors to the tuberculin test for tuberculosis, in each year mentioned;
3.	The amount paid as compensation for pure bred registered cattle, and average payment per head. Also showing the same information for grade cattle;
4.	The total amount paid in each year in
salaries, wages and travelling expenses1 to offi-cials_ of the Department of Agriculture in connection with the administration of the tuberculin test for cattle in the province of Nova Scotia;
5.	The total amount paid in each year, in salaries, wages and travelling expenses to officials of the Department of Agriculture, in connection with the administration of the tuberculin test throughout the Dominion for the years ending March 31, 1924, 1925, 1926, 1927, and 1928.
